      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "An L-shaped figure is formed by removing a $2$ cm $\\times$ $3$ cm rectangle from the corner of a $6$ cm $\\times$ $5$ cm rectangle. What is the perimeter of the L-shape?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$26$ cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$22$ cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$32$ cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$16$ cm"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "Trace around the L-shape: the six sides are $6$, $5$, $4$, $3$, $2$, and $2$ cm. Total perimeter $= 6 + 5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 2 = 22$ cm."
